<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Welcome to Blowfish! :tada: on CurrySIN's Station</title><link>https://currysinhk.github.io/blog/</link><description>Recent content in Welcome to Blowfish! :tada: on CurrySIN's Station</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><copyright>© 2026 Curry SIN</copyright><lastBuildDate>Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://currysinhk.github.io/blog/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Illustrated Catalog: Guide and Usage</title><link>https://currysinhk.github.io/blog/posts/tech-things/catalog-guide/</link><pubDate>Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://currysinhk.github.io/blog/posts/tech-things/catalog-guide/</guid><description>&lt;div class="lead text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 !mb-9 text-xl"&gt;
The &lt;strong&gt;catalog&lt;/strong&gt; supports single entries or &lt;strong&gt;collections with multiple sub-items&lt;/strong&gt;. Images come from publicly shared Google Drive links.
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;What is the catalog?
&lt;div id="what-is-the-catalog" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;span
class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100"&gt;
&lt;a class="group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700"
style="text-decoration-line: none !important;" href="#what-is-the-catalog" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Separate from blog &lt;strong&gt;posts&lt;/strong&gt;. Use it for typed image collections, structured metadata, and Drive-hosted images (no large files in Git).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;strong&gt;Catalog&lt;/strong&gt; in the menu: &lt;code&gt;/catalog/&lt;/code&gt; (with language prefixes, e.g. &lt;code&gt;/zh-tw/catalog/&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Apache Lincense Version 2.0</title><link>https://currysinhk.github.io/blog/posts/tech-things/apache/license-2/</link><pubDate>Wed, 24 Apr 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://currysinhk.github.io/blog/posts/tech-things/apache/license-2/</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Terminology
